# Change Log

2026-10-15
- Synced all open Dependabot updates into one branch (merged the branches of PRs #101-#105, #111, #113, #116, #118) so they land together with the follow-up fixes below; those PRs can be closed once this merges.
- Release 11.0.3: bumped all version references from 10.4.3. parsedmarc 11.0.0 made the output and mailbox integrations optional extras (upstream #883), so a plain `parsedmarc==11.x` install has no Elasticsearch/OpenSearch/Kafka/S3/Graph/Gmail clients. Dependabot's #116 only changed the pin, which would have built green and failed at runtime for every Graph or Elasticsearch user. All images now install `parsedmarc[all]` (`requirements.in`, `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.hardened`); `urllib3>=2.8.0` (#113).
- Fixed `scheduled-secure-images`: it took the version from the latest GitHub release (still 10.2.1, since 10.4.3 had no release), so every scheduled run rebuilt and repushed `:latest`/`:distroless` from parsedmarc 10.2.1 and overwrote the immutable `:10.2.1`/`:10.2.1-distroless` tags. It now reads the version from `requirements.in`, validates it, pushes only the floating `latest`/`distroless` tags, and signs by digest. The `workflow_dispatch` input is passed through an env var instead of being interpolated into the shell script.
- Snyk Container failures (2026-10-01, 2026-10-08): Alpine images flagged `util-linux/libuuid` 2.41.4-r0 (fixed in 2.41.6). Replaced the pinned packages pulled from Alpine **edge** (`zlib=1.3.2-r0`, `musl=1.2.5-r23`, `openssl`) with `apk upgrade --no-cache` on the stable branch: mixing edge `musl` into a 3.23 image is unsupported, and exact edge pins break the build as soon as edge moves on. Bumped base digests: `python:3.14-alpine3.23` -> `e7cff362`, `debian:trixie-slim` -> `a29215f6`, `distroless/python3-debian13:nonroot` -> `83aa8d4f` (Debian sqlite/expat findings), `ubi9/python-312` -> `40578f84` (#118). `Dockerfile` now uses `python:3.14-alpine3.23` instead of `python:3-alpine3.23`, which started tracking Python 3.15.
- Not verified locally: image builds could not be run in the sandbox used for this change; the PR's Docker Build Check / build-locked-commit runs are the verification.

2026-08-25
- Fixed `build-locked-commit`/`build-locked-release` failures (broken since the 2026-08-15 scheduled run): `pip-tools==7.5.3` is incompatible with pip 26.2 (`make_requirement_preparer() missing 'allow_editables'`). Bumped `PIP_TOOLS_VERSION` to 7.6.1 in both workflows; verified locally that pip-compile 7.6.1 + pip 26.2.1 resolves `requirements.in` (parsedmarc 10.4.3) with hashes.
- Addressed the failing scheduled Snyk Container Scan (all 5 images) by bumping every base image digest: `python:3-alpine3.23`/`python:3.14-alpine3.23` -> `6b8f06d0` and added `sqlite-libs` to `apk add --upgrade` (plain `apk add` is a no-op for already-installed packages) (sqlite heap overflows SNYK-ALPINE323-SQLITE-18913461/2, fixed in 3.53.4-r0 now in v3.23 main); `python:3.14-slim-trixie` -> `83ff1d24` and `distroless/python3-debian13:nonroot` -> `6bfc400d` (ships `libexpat1 2.8.3-1~deb13u1`, verified via dpkg status.d — resolves CVE-2026-45186, removed from SECURITY.md accepted risks); `ubi9/python-312` -> `2d3e2a70` (targets the `libcurl-minimal` 7.76.1-40.el9 findings; UBI html.parser/tar accepted risks to be re-checked on the post-push Snyk scan).
- Found and fixed a pre-existing runtime breakage in both distroless images (`Dockerfile.hardened` `:distroless` tag and `Dockerfile-debian.locked` `-debian` locked tag): the venv was built with the docker-official python 3.14 (`/usr/local/bin/python3.14`), which does not exist in `gcr.io/distroless/python3-debian13` (Debian python 3.13 at `/usr/bin`), so `exec /opt/venv/bin/parsedmarc` failed with "no such file or directory" — confirmed the already-published `:distroless` image had the same failure. Switched both builder stages to `debian:trixie-slim` + apt `python3`/`python3-venv` so interpreter path and ABI (3.13) match the runtime stage; verified the rebuilt image runs (`--version` -> 10.4.3).
- Manually dispatched Snyk Container Scan after the remediation push: `locked-alpine` and `locked-debian` now pass. `latest` and `distroless` floating tags failed only because they still pointed at old images — re-pushed both from the rebuilt 10.4.3 images. `locked-ubi` still fails: Red Hat has no fixed curl packages (base bump only moved curl to 7.76.1-40.el9_8.5); documented the 5 curl/libcurl CVE pairs as an accepted risk in SECURITY.md (curl is healthcheck-only in that image, parsedmarc never links libcurl).
- PR triage per standing policy: closed #100 (parsedmarc 10.4.1, superseded by the 10.4.3 bump on main), closed #89-#95 (Dependabot branches from Jul 14, >30 days stale; Dependabot will re-propose current versions), closed #99 (ubi9 digest `ebd0347`, superseded by the newer `2d3e2a70` bump on main).
- Release 10.4.3: bumped all version references (`requirements.in`, `Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.hardened`, `docker-compose.yml`, `build.sh`, `docker-image.yml`) from 10.2.1 to 10.4.3. Locked variants need no edit — CI regenerates `requirements.lock` from `requirements.in`.
- Fixed a local-build failure introduced by 10.4.x's new source-only deps (`dkimpy`, `authres`): the `ARG SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH=""` default leaks an empty env var into `RUN`, and setuptools/wheel does `int(os.environ["SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH"])` while building sdists, crashing with `ValueError: invalid literal for int()`. Added an `unset`-when-empty guard before `pip install` in `Dockerfile` and `Dockerfile.hardened` (reproduced and confirmed the root cause in a local venv). CI passes a real epoch, so this only affected builds without one.
- Built `ghcr.io/mkilijanek/parsedmarc:10.4.3` locally, smoke-tested (`--version` prints 10.4.3), and pushed to GHCR (digest `sha256:7c600747c077ab3801b9277d3f0d9bf495fedfd673e672dd3dd94ed5c58a707e`) after refreshing the `gh` token with the `write:packages` scope.

2026-07-13
- Documented two newly-disclosed CVEs found in a manual re-scan of the `-ubi` locked image as accepted risks in `SECURITY.md`: `CVE-2026-15308` (`python3`/`python3.12` `html.parser` CPU DoS) and `CVE-2026-59873`/`CVE-2026-59874` (`tar` unbounded resource use / stalled loop DoS). Traced both against parsedmarc's actual code paths: `mailsuite.utils.parse_email()` (the only caller of `html2text`/`html.parser` in the dependency tree) is never invoked by this codebase, and `tarfile`/the `tar` binary are never used (report attachments go through `zipfile`/gzip only) — so both are present-but-unreachable rather than exploitable. No fixed RHEL9 packages exist yet for either.

2026-07-10
- Release 10.2.1: bumped all version references (`Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.hardened`, `docker-compose.yml`, `build.sh`, `docker-image.yml`) from 10.2.0 to 10.2.1 to match `requirements.in`.
- Added `curl` to `Dockerfile` (default alpine image) and `Dockerfile-alpine.locked` via `apk add curl`. Left `Dockerfile-ubi.locked` alone (already has a working `curl` from the `curl-minimal` package kept for dnf/rpm) and left `Dockerfile-debian.locked`/`Dockerfile.hardened` alone (distroless, no package manager). Re-released the `10.2.1` tag/images to include this change.
- Documented `CVE-2026-45186` (`expat`/`libexpat1` algorithmic complexity DoS, affects `Dockerfile.hardened` and `Dockerfile-debian.locked`) as an accepted risk in `SECURITY.md`: no fixed `expat` package exists yet for Debian trixie, and the distroless final stage has no package manager to pin around it. Re-check on the next `distroless/python3-debian13` base digest bump.

2026-07-08
- Merged all 8 open Dependabot PRs: `parsedmarc` 9.11.2 -> 10.2.0, distroless/python3-debian13 and ubi9/python-312 base digest bumps, and 5 GitHub Actions version bumps (`docker/login-action`, `docker/metadata-action`, `docker/build-push-action`, `docker/setup-buildx-action`, `github/codeql-action`). The base-image bumps also resolved the `expat/libexpat1` CVE that was failing the scheduled Snyk Container Scan on the `locked-debian` image.
- Added a 14-day (`*/14 * *`) schedule to `build-locked-release` so the floating `alpine`/`debian`/`ubi` locked image tags get rebuilt against current base images even without a push to `main`. Pinned per-release version tags remain untouched/immutable.
- Fixed a stale hardcoded fallback (`9.2.1`) in `scheduled-secure-images`: it now resolves the latest published GitHub release dynamically when no version is supplied, and only pushes the floating `latest`/`distroless` tags (it was previously also repushing content under the immutable per-version tag on every scheduled run). Cadence changed from weekly to every 14 days.
- Release 10.2.0: bumped all version references (`Dockerfile`, `Dockerfile.hardened`, `docker-compose.yml`, `build.sh`, `docker-image.yml`) from 9.11.2 to 10.2.0 to match `requirements.in`.

2026-05-25
- Release 9.11.2: bumped all version references from 9.5.4/9.6.0 to 9.11.2 across Dockerfiles, docker-compose.yml, build.sh, requirements.in, and CI workflows.
- Consolidated and applied all 10 open Dependabot dependency bumps:
  * `parsedmarc` 9.6.0 -> 9.11.2 (requirements.in + lock rebuild) for latest fixes.
  * `urllib3` >=2.6.3 -> >=2.7.0 to pick up security patches.
